{"data": [{"author_id": "612896910", "created_at": "2026-11-07T16:15:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119101319512281127"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 90, "start": 82, "tag": "BLSdata"}], "urls": [{"description": "The .gov means it's official. Federal government websites often end in .gov or .mil. Before sharing sensitive information, make sure you're on a federal government site. The site is secure. The https:// ensures that you are connecting to the official website and that any information you provide is encrypted and transmitted securely. In 2025, average annual consumer expenditures increased by 4.3 percent from 2024. Average annual income increased by 6.4 percent. Consumer spending on food was up by 4.6", "display_url": "bls.gov/opub/ted/2026/…", "end": 81, "expanded_url": "https://www.bls.gov/opub/ted/2026/consumer-spending-increased-4-3-percent-from-2024-to-2025.htm", "images": [{"height": 126, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2118744396791255040/TIeKvkMG?format=png&name=orig", "width": 228}, {"height": 126, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2118744396791255040/TIeKvkMG?format=png&name=150x150", "width": 126}], "start": 58, "status": 200, "title": "Consumer spending increased 4.3 percent from 2024 to 2025 : The Economics Daily : U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics", "unwound_url": "https://www.bls.gov/opub/ted/2026/consumer-spending-increased-4-3-percent-from-2024-to-2025.htm", "url": "https://t.co/HaCUkYFiSO"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/rXseyTInsl", "end": 114, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/BLS_gov/status/2119101319512281127/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2118816670823194624", "start": 91, "url": "https://t.co/rXseyTInsl"}]}, "id": "2119101319512281127", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 2, "impression_count": 2978, "like_count": 13, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 4, "retweet_count": 3}, "text": "Consumer spending increased 4.3 percent from 2024 to 2025 https://t.co/HaCUkYFiSO #BLSdata https://t.co/rXseyTInsl", "url": "https://x.com/BLS_gov/status/2119101319512281127"}, {"author_id": "39125788", "created_at": "2026-11-07T15:03:19.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119083280381383072"], "id": "2119083280381383072", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 219, "impression_count": 58924, "like_count": 1024, "quote_count": 33, "reply_count": 202, "retweet_count": 94}, "text": "This can be a golden age of investigative journalism. Analyzing filings, records and public data to go deep into a company or government or whatever used to be something that took a team of journalists a long time, so was relatively rare. Now LLMs can 10x investigative research.", "url": "https://x.com/emollick/status/2119083280381383072"}, {"author_id": "83466368", "created_at": "2026-11-07T14:00:58.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119067590731649153"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 101, "id": "304909941", "start": 93, "username": "Lagarde"}], "urls": [{"description": "The European Central Bank (ECB) is the central bank of the European Union countries which have adopted the euro. Our main task is to maintain price stability in the euro area and so preserve the purchasing power of the single currency.", "display_url": "ecb.europa.eu/press/inter/da…", "end": 276, "expanded_url": "https://www.ecb.europa.eu/press/inter/date/2026/html/ecb.in261107~e7b86fc4ce.en.html", "images": [{"height": 600, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2119067606875602944/8qf1e5Um?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1200}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2119067606875602944/8qf1e5Um?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 253, "status": 200, "title": "Interview with Yomiuri Shimbun", "unwound_url": "https://www.ecb.europa.eu/press/inter/date/2026/html/ecb.in261107~e7b86fc4ce.en.html", "url": "https://t.co/YIUMvd9mF3"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/6HFIp8xVFz", "end": 300, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/ecb/status/2119067590731649153/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2119067583693340675", "start": 277, "url": "https://t.co/6HFIp8xVFz"}]}, "id": "2119067590731649153", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 17, "impression_count": 21042, "like_count": 133, "quote_count": 14, "reply_count": 50, "retweet_count": 26}, "text": "Energy is pushing up inflation numbers and food inflation has also increased, says President @Lagarde. \n\nBut the underlying indicators are stable and we are currently not seeing signs of second-round effects beyond those incorporated in our projections https://t.co/YIUMvd9mF3 https://t.co/6HFIp8xVFz", "url": "https://x.com/ecb/status/2119067590731649153"}, {"author_id": "332617373", "created_at": "2026-11-07T12:59:34.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2119052139410403410"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/MjC5rNPgEZ", "end": 303, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/elerianm/status/2119052139410403410/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2119052135811694593", "start": 280, "url": "https://t.co/MjC5rNPgEZ"}]}, "id": "2119052139410403410", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 12, "impression_count": 34443, "like_count": 457, "quote_count": 8, "reply_count": 23, "retweet_count": 56}, "text": "These photos, which just popped up on my phone, are a wonderful reminder of my first visit to the \"57357\" Children’s Cancer Hospital in Egypt almost ten years ago.\nThe hospital delivers world-class cancer treatment and cure to children completely free of charge to them and their https://t.co/MjC5rNPgEZ", "url": "https://x.com/elerianm/status/2119052139410403410"}, {"author_id": "1214528593", "created_at": "2026-11-07T09:28:00.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118998896500461633"], "id": "2118998896500461633", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 2, "impression_count": 4411, "like_count": 76, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 13, "retweet_count": 5}, "text": "Highly persistent internal model?\n\nYou mean a model with a little bit of enthusiasm, a little bit of energy, and a little bit of stick it to 'em?", "url": "https://x.com/Miles_Brundage/status/2118998896500461633"}, {"author_id": "39125788", "created_at": "2026-11-07T05:41:12.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118941821740953637"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/3h2P7PFaDK", "end": 304, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/emollick/status/2118941821740953637/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2118940824457125888", "start": 281, "url": "https://t.co/3h2P7PFaDK"}]}, "id": "2118941821740953637", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 78, "impression_count": 70366, "like_count": 378, "quote_count": 18, "reply_count": 104, "retweet_count": 32}, "text": "As a longtime reader (and writer of two small pieces in the 1990s) of WIRED, I was curious if the coverage of the AI era really does differ from its coverage of the early internet. A couple of experiments with Astra shows it does. Interpretation depends on your view of AI, though https://t.co/3h2P7PFaDK", "url": "https://x.com/emollick/status/2118941821740953637"}, {"author_id": "39125788", "created_at": "2026-11-07T00:14:27.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118859591798980657"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "In this report, we use privacy-preserving infrastructure to study the scientific use of Claude, Claude Code, and Claude Science. We document how usage varies across scientific fields and research tasks, identify what explains these usage patterns, and outline scenarios for how AI could accelerate research.", "display_url": "anthropic.com/research/how-r…", "end": 276, "expanded_url": "https://www.anthropic.com/research/how-researchers-use-claude", "images": [{"height": 630, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2118374238356738048/BOjucj91?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1200}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2118374238356738048/BOjucj91?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 253, "status": 200, "title": "How scientists use Claude", "unwound_url": "https://www.anthropic.com/research/how-researchers-use-claude", "url": "https://t.co/1FOHn2l5Xr"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/YCb48MWo4H", "end": 300, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/emollick/status/2118859591798980657/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2118857543317352449", "start": 277, "url": "https://t.co/YCb48MWo4H"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/YCb48MWo4H", "end": 300, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/emollick/status/2118859591798980657/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2118859515013586944", "start": 277, "url": "https://t.co/YCb48MWo4H"}]}, "id": "2118859591798980657", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 375, "impression_count": 57806, "like_count": 695, "quote_count": 33, "reply_count": 189, "retweet_count": 102}, "text": "Some new data from Anthropic looking at the impact of AI on the sciences by field: \"With current capabilities, if adopted widely, AI could take on 27–52% of the researcher time needed to produce a new study, with a median of 38% across fields...\"\nHere: https://t.co/1FOHn2l5Xr https://t.co/YCb48MWo4H", "url": "https://x.com/emollick/status/2118859591798980657"}, {"author_id": "279036722", "created_at": "2026-11-06T22:29:03.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118833064109633579"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/jonsteinsson/s…", "end": 35, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/jonsteinsson/status/2118804376727015660", "start": 12, "url": "https://t.co/omN5jnbb52"}]}, "id": "2118833064109633579", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 77, "impression_count": 40512, "like_count": 157, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 8, "retweet_count": 10}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118804376727015660", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Intriguing. https://t.co/omN5jnbb52", "url": "https://x.com/jasonfurman/status/2118833064109633579"}, {"author_id": "1214528593", "created_at": "2026-11-06T22:16:42.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118829955618664463"], "id": "2118829955618664463", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 15, "impression_count": 4681, "like_count": 59, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 6, "retweet_count": 4}, "text": "A big part of the idea behind third party evaluation/auditing is that the identity and biases of an org doing the analysis are important, otherwise we’d take the companies’ word for it or require full transparency.\n\nEven without full info, the METR report is very notable because", "url": "https://x.com/Miles_Brundage/status/2118829955618664463"}, {"author_id": "26538229", "created_at": "2026-11-06T21:18:38.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118815345288921567"], "entities": {"hashtags": [{"end": 119, "start": 111, "tag": "FedData"}], "urls": [{"description": "The Federal Reserve Board of Governors in Washington DC.", "display_url": "federalreserve.gov/releases/h8/cu…", "end": 143, "expanded_url": "https://federalreserve.gov/releases/h8/current/default.htm", "images": [{"height": 800, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2118815388657958912/Ou6kRA_D?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 800}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2118815388657958912/Ou6kRA_D?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 120, "status": 200, "title": "Lock", "unwound_url": "https://www.federalreserve.gov/releases/h8/current/default.htm", "url": "https://t.co/WeJhdaAjBV"}]}, "id": "2118815345288921567", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 21, "impression_count": 46650, "like_count": 106, "quote_count": 2, "reply_count": 19, "retweet_count": 27}, "text": "Now available: Weekly data on the H.8 release, Assets and Liabilities of Commercial Banks in the United States #FedData https://t.co/WeJhdaAjBV", "url": "https://x.com/federalreserve/status/2118815345288921567"}], "includes": {"users": [{"id": "612896910", "name": "BLS-Labor Statistics", "username": "BLS_gov"}, {"id": "39125788", "name": "Ethan Mollick", "username": "emollick"}, {"id": "83466368", "name": "European Central Bank", "username": "ecb"}, {"id": "332617373", "name": "Mohamed A. El-Erian", "username": "elerianm"}, {"id": "1214528593", "name": "Miles Brundage", "username": "Miles_Brundage"}, {"id": "279036722", "name": "Jason Furman", "username": "jasonfurman"}, {"id": "26538229",